# THE BIGSHOT — Project Instructions

Before making changes to this project, read `GAME_MASTER_PROMPT.md` completely.

Treat it as the main game vision, design specification and development roadmap.

## How to work

- Inspect the existing repository, game engine, code, assets and build process before making changes.
- Preserve working features and integrate new systems into the existing project.
- Work autonomously. Make sensible decisions and add useful features that fit the game's vision.
- Build connected, playable systems rather than disconnected menus, placeholders or mock functionality.
- Follow the milestones, feature dependencies, asset requirements and animation requirements in the master prompt.
- Test actual gameplay, saves, loading, economy behaviour and integrations wherever possible.
- Fix discovered bugs and regressions before moving on.
- Keep documentation, the roadmap and implementation status up to date.
- Never claim something is implemented or tested unless it genuinely is.
- If a tool, asset or capability is unavailable, explain the limitation and use a sensible alternative.
- Prioritise a working, playable game and continue development beyond initial planning.

## Starting work

Read the master prompt and inspect the repository. Identify the current state of the project, then implement the highest-priority missing milestone. Do not stop after producing a plan. Make changes, test them and report what actually works.

The project title is currently **THE BIGSHOT** and may change later.
